HUGE finding: `decode(File, {at: At})` is today's answer to dot access. Relation-valued columns (`repo: repo`), struct columns, and decode patterns already implement "navigation" — via pattern destructuring (Souffle style), not dot. The `dcoord` example is literally `span.file.at.name` written as two decode joins. This is the "dot path is a join chain" ruling (lab-assimilation-sweep W4 SUPERSEDED) made real in the shipped compiler.

